        "id": 18995,
        "name": "Obsidian Lukahn",
        "username": "Obsidian_Lukahn",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/o/258eb7/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-04T23:34:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>** warning: minor spoilers for the Stolen Legacy issue **</p>\n<p>Last night I just started running my kids + neighbor kids through the Stolen Legacy issue. As we progressed through the first scene in the park, the heroes were being attacked by the web ghosts and skeletons, and Headlong gets into the yellow zone, where he began using Bowl Over. Not quite sure how I'm supposed to handle an ability that allowed him to attack multiple targets, I allowed him to attack *all* the minions, but after the fact that seemed a bit overpowered based on other actions which only allow one target, or multiple targets needing a minor twist. Especially since there isn't any downside to actually using the ability.</p>\n<p>Maybe I missed something in the current rules as written, but the ability doesn't mention needing to take a minor twist so I'm assuming that isn't required the way it would be if it was a basic action targeting multiple targets. I'm also concerned about the power of this ability since other abilities that target multiple targets, such as Aeon Girl's Internal Cataclysm have some minor negative attached to them.</p>\n<p>Since there isn't any guidance about what \"multiple targets\" means, is this just something that needs to be ruled on a case-by-case basis? If, for instance, the web ghosts were up in the air \"in flight\", I'd assume he wouldn't be able to bowl them over. The skeletons were slightly scattered because they were all attacking each hero, but it seemed like a pretty heroic bit of awesomeness to allow Headlong to fly past each one and hit them. But then Rockstar's single smash abilities&nbsp;didn't seem nearly as impressive after that.</p>\n<p>Any thoughts on how mutliple targets should be handled? I haven't been able to find much discussion about it, particularly Headlong's ability.</p>\n<p>-OL</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:31.898Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
