        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/4bbf92/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-12T11:54:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>One guideline I see often to this frequent question is the following.</p>\n<p>The player's action should be limited to one frame of a comic book.</p>\n<p>For me hitting a large group of targets would need a large panel. As a rule of thumb I can imagine nearly an infinite amount of minions being taken ito it isn't the last frame of the battle, but if the rest of the battle is still going on then perhaps reduce it to 3 or 4.</p>\n<p>Of course each GM (editor) had their own esthetics.</p>",
